The query in `2result.sql` is the best choice:

• It cleanly isolates the qualifying bowlers in a single CTE (`qualifying_bowlers`), ensuring each one has at least one ≤ 190 win at all three required venues before any rows are returned.  
• The final SELECT then simply filters to those bowlers and the three venues, returning exactly the requested columns.  
• Compared with `0result.sql` (nested sub‑query that is harder to read) and `1result.sql` (two CTEs doing extra work), `2result.sql` is the most concise while still fully satisfying every rule.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```
